{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2170-09-19 13:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee, one of the surgical team members. You're here today for your scheduled gastrostomy tube placement, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2170-09-19 13:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. I’ve been having so much nausea and trouble keeping food down. I hope this helps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2170-09-19 13:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. This tube will help transition you from TPN to tube feedings, which should be easier on your system. The procedure is done by interventional radiology, and you’ll be back here afterward."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2170-09-19 13:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I feel anything during the procedure?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2170-09-19 13:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll get sedation—fentanyl and Versed—so you’ll be drowsy and comfortable. Your vital signs will be closely watched the whole time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2170-09-19 13:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds okay. And the tube goes into my stomach?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2170-09-19 13:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, into the gastric remnant—your stomach pouch from the bypass. It’s placed under fluoroscopy, so they can see exactly where it goes. It’s a minimally invasive procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2170-09-19 13:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I’ll start feeds right away?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2170-09-19 13:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not immediately. We’ll start with clear liquids by mouth tomorrow to make sure you tolerate that. Then, after 24 hours, we’ll begin tube feeds slowly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2170-09-19 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my PICC line—will that stay in?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2170-09-19 13:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll remove it once you’re tolerating tube feeds well. Since you’re on TPN now, we’ll keep it until we’re sure the tube feeding is working."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2170-09-19 13:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. I’ve been on TPN for a while, but it’s not ideal long-term."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2170-09-19 13:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. The goal is to get you off TPN and onto enteral nutrition, which is safer and more natural for your gut."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2170-09-19 15:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re back! The procedure went smoothly. The tube is in place, and the chest X-ray confirms it’s positioned correctly in your stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2170-09-19 15:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. Does it hurt? I feel a little pressure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2170-09-19 15:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Some mild tenderness is normal. We’ll give you pain meds if needed. The site is dressed and secured with sutures. We’ll keep an eye on it for any signs of infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2170-09-19 15:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the PICC is still in?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2170-09-19 15:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, still in. We’ll continue your TPN and IV pantoprazole for now. Tomorrow, we’ll start you on clear liquids by mouth."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2170-09-20 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling? Any nausea or pain at the tube site?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2170-09-20 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little sore, but not bad. I had some water last night and kept it down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2170-09-20 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. We’ll start advancing your diet today. First, clear liquids, then if you do well, we’ll begin tube feeds this afternoon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2170-09-20 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What kind of formula will I get through the tube?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2170-09-20 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re starting with ‘Replete with Fiber’—it’s balanced and includes fiber to help with bowel regularity. It’ll run at 110 mL per hour for 12 hours overnight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2170-09-20 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I’ll still take my regular meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2170-09-20 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, all your home meds—aripiprazole, citalopram, lamotrigine, lorazepam, nortriptyline, temazepam, and pantoprazole. We’ll switch pantoprazole to oral today since you can swallow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2170-09-20 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re starting your tube feeds now. We’ll begin slowly and monitor for any nausea or bloating."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2170-09-20 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Should I feel anything?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2170-09-20 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You might feel a little fullness, but not pain. Let us know if you feel nauseous or crampy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2170-09-20 20:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well—no nausea, and the feeds are going at goal rate. We’re going to try advancing you to a regular diet tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2170-09-20 20:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Really? I haven’t eaten solid food in weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2170-09-20 20:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start with small amounts. If you tolerate it, you can eat more. Your nausea has improved, which is a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2170-09-21 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You had a good night—feeds completed, no issues. We removed the PICC line this morning since you’re stable on enteral nutrition."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2170-09-21 07:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. I was worried about infections from the line."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2170-09-21 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Now we focus on your recovery at home. You’ll continue the tube feeds overnight and take pantoprazole daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2170-09-21 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the pain med?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2170-09-21 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Oxycodone-acetaminophen as needed. But use it sparingly—your pain is mild, and we want you off opioids quickly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2170-09-21 07:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. What about follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2170-09-21 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll see surgery in two weeks. Also, continue with gastroenterology—they’re managing your cyclic vomiting syndrome with nortriptyline."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2170-09-21 07:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the tube care at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2170-09-21 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep the site clean and dry. Wash with soapy water daily. Watch for redness, swelling, or discharge. Call if you have fever or worsening pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2170-09-21 07:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And can I shower?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2170-09-21 07:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but keep the site dry—use a waterproof cover. No baths or swimming for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2170-09-21 07:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll be careful. I’m ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2170-09-21 07:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll get the discharge papers ready. You’re doing great—tolerating feeds, walking, and pain controlled. You’ll go home with a nurse visit to help with the pump."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2170-09-21 07:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’m hopeful this will help me eat better and gain weight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2170-09-21 07:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We are too. The goal is improved nutrition and fewer hospital visits. Keep up the good work."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2170-09-21 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a final check before discharge. Your labs are stable—hemoglobin, electrolytes, kidney function—all good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2170-09-21 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s reassuring. And my malnutrition?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2170-09-21 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "This tube is the key. With consistent feeds, your nutrition should improve over the next few weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2170-09-21 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll stick to the plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2170-09-21 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. Remember: call if you vomit, can’t keep fluids down, have chest pain, or fever over 101.5."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2170-09-21 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2170-09-21 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll see you in follow-up. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2170-09-21 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The enteral infusion is running smoothly. You’ve reached goal rate. We’re documenting this as part of your discharge process."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2170-09-21 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It feels normal. I didn’t even notice it started."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2170-09-21 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s ideal. Means your body is adjusting well. You’re ready for discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2170-09-21 12:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad. I feel like I can manage this at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2170-09-21 12:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re confident too. Just follow the instructions, and you’ll do well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2170-09-21 12:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2170-09-21 12:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you soon."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2170-09-19 13:21:00",
    "admission_end": "2170-09-21 13:05:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for planned gastrostomy tube placement to transition from parenteral to enteral nutrition due to chronic nausea, poor oral intake, and malnutrition following bariatric surgery. The procedure was performed under fluoroscopic guidance and completed without complications. Post-procedure, she tolerated clear liquids and was advanced to goal tube feeds within 24 hours. Her nausea improved, and she also tolerated a regular diet. The PICC line was removed, and she remained afebrile with stable vital signs. She was discharged home on enteral nutrition with a Zevex Infinity Pump, oral pantoprazole, and home medications, including nortriptyline for cyclic vomiting syndrome. Discharge instructions included tube site care, activity restrictions, and close symptom monitoring.",
    "problems": [
      "Unspecified protein-calorie malnutrition",
      "Polycystic ovaries",
      "Bariatric surgery status"
    ]
  }
}
